{
 "about": "Shared argv rules (dt21 round 3). Each case is an argv array (MCP server args, element 0 the command) or a command string. 'secrets' are the credential values (exact substrings) the probe disguises, the report masker masks and MCP-003 reports; 'keep' are elements or substrings that must stay as written. Rules: (1) a following element is a flag, not a value, only when flag-shaped (^--?[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_-]*$ AND the name after the dashes does not look random: looksRandom(name, 12) false, so -Xq9Zr7Lm2Pv8Kd4Wb6Tn3Hc is a value while -v, -pthread, --no-auth are flags) or exactly '--' (end of options; what follows is a positional, no flag's value); any other '-'-led element is a value. (2) -p<v> glued after a password client (mysql, mysqldump, mariadb, mariadb-dump, mysqladmin, sshpass) is a password unless a reference; a separate -p <v> is one only after sshpass (MySQL/MariaDB take the password glued: in mysql -p app_db the client prompts and app_db is the database); psql/pg_dump/redis-cli -p is a port; anywhere else (a MySQL client's separate -p included) -p <v> is a password only when v looks like a credential (MCP-003's looksLikeSecret) and is no port, port mapping, version, package spec, reference or lowercase word; a MySQL/MariaDB client's --password=<v> is its password like a glued -p<v>. (3) -k <v> is a credential when v looks random (looksRandom, 16) and is no URL, host[:port] or path (isPathValue); '/' and '+' inside do not exclude it. (4) redis-cli -a <v> is a password unless a reference. (5) curl -u/--user/--proxy-user (separate, or --user=/--proxy-user=) user:password: the part after the first colon is the password unless empty or a reference; another command's -u (docker -u 1000:1000, --user app:app) is not judged. --pw and --pass are credential flags like --password. (6) MYSQL_PWD=<v>, PGPASSWORD=<v>, SSHPASS=<v>, REDISCLI_AUTH=<v> (a client's password variable) hold a password unless a reference. (7) Other clients' password options take any stored value, separate or glued (short) / separate or = (long): sqlcmd -P/-z/-Z and bcp -P; docker/podman/nerdctl/buildah/skopeo/oras login and helm registry login -p/--password; smbclient/rpcclient/smbcacls/smbcquotas -U/--user user%password (after the first %) and --password; lftp -u user,password (after the first comma); ldapsearch/ldapadd/ldapmodify/ldapdelete/ldapmodrdn/ldapcompare/ldapwhoami/ldapexop -w (ldappasswd also -a/-s); mongo/mongosh/mongodump/mongorestore/mongoexport/mongoimport/mongostat/mongotop/mongofiles -p/--password (a URL value is the server: mongosh -p <url> prompts); htpasswd -b's password argument (file user password; with -n user password); a FreeRDP client's /p:<pw> (2.x /gp:<pw>). '-' (read stdin) and references are not passwords. (8) What echo or printf (its arguments, or its format when it has no %) pipes into sudo -S/--stdin or a registry login with --password-stdin / --password - is the password. In a command string the words are what the shell assembles: quotes around or inside a word are the shell's at any depth of escaping, quoted and unquoted parts written together are one word ('-p'\"pw\" is -ppw, \"-ppw\" is -ppw), a quote opened inside a word runs to its closing quote across spaces (-p\"pass phrase\": the password is 'pass phrase'), a quoted string after a flag is its argument (sshpass -p \"a b\"), $'...' is ANSI-C quoting anywhere in a word, and commands are split at ; && || & and at | (a pipeline's commands are judged apart, rule 8 across them).",
 "segments": [
  {"line": "mysql -u root \"-pPw\" app", "words": [["mysql", "-u", "root", "-pPw", "app"]]},
  {"line": "mysql '-p'\"Pw\" app", "words": [["mysql", "-pPw", "app"]]},
  {"line": "mysql -p\"pass phrase\" app", "words": [["mysql", "-ppass phrase", "app"]]},
  {"line": "\"command\": \"mysql -p\\\"pass phrase\\\" app\"", "words": [["command:"], ["mysql", "-ppass phrase", "app"]]},
  {"line": "mysql --password=${DB_PASSWORD} \"$(pass)\" app", "words": [["mysql", "--password=${DB_PASSWORD}", "$(pass)", "app"]]},
  {"line": "mysql -p$'Pw' app", "words": [["mysql", "-pPw", "app"]]},
  {"line": "mysql -p$'a\\x41\\tb' app", "words": [["mysql", "-paA\tb", "app"]]},
  {"line": "mysql -p$\"Pw\" app", "words": [["mysql", "-pPw", "app"]]},
  {"line": "\"command\": \"sshpass -p $\\\"Pw\\\" ssh h\"", "words": [["command:"], ["sshpass", "-p", "Pw", "ssh", "h"]]},
  {"line": "\"command\": \"mysql -p$\\\"P w\\\" app\"", "words": [["command:"], ["mysql", "-pP w", "app"]]},
  {"line": "sshpass -p \"a b\" ssh h", "words": [["sshpass", "-p", "a b"], ["a", "b"], ["ssh", "h"]]},
  {"line": "sh -c 'mysql -pX app && psql -p 5432 db'", "words": [["sh", "-c", "mysql -pX app && psql -p 5432 db"], ["mysql", "-pX", "app"], ["psql", "-p", "5432", "db"]]},
  {"line": "echo pw | sudo -S true; ls", "words": [["echo", "pw"], ["sudo", "-S", "true"], ["ls"]], "pipes": [true, false, false]},
  {"line": "\"args\": [\"-p\", \"Xk9\"]", "words": [["args:"], ["-p"], ["Xk9"]]}
 ],
 "cases": [
  {"name": "dash-led value after a credential flag", "argv": ["acme", "--api-key", "-Xq9Zr7Lm2Pv8Kd4Wb6Tn3Hc"], "secrets": ["-Xq9Zr7Lm2Pv8Kd4Wb6Tn3Hc"], "keep": ["--api-key"]},
  {"name": "dash-led password", "argv": ["acme", "--password", "-Pz9Lm2Qr7Xv4Kt8Wn3Yb5"], "secrets": ["-Pz9Lm2Qr7Xv4Kt8Wn3Yb5"], "keep": ["--password"]},
  {"name": "secret-named switch before the credential flag", "argv": ["acme", "--no-auth", "--api-key", "Xq9Zr7Lm2Pv8Kd4Wb6Tn3Hc"], "secrets": ["Xq9Zr7Lm2Pv8Kd4Wb6Tn3Hc"], "keep": ["--no-auth", "--api-key"]},
  {"name": "two credential flags in a row", "argv": ["acme", "--token", "--api-key", "Xq9Zr7Lm2Pv8Kd4Wb6Tn3Hd"], "secrets": ["Xq9Zr7Lm2Pv8Kd4Wb6Tn3Hd"], "keep": ["--token", "--api-key"]},
  {"name": "credential flag followed by a short flag", "argv": ["acme", "--token", "-v", "server.js"], "secrets": [], "keep": ["--token", "-v", "server.js"]},
